# Regression test: follow-up to struct_custom_remove_call_site.br (`ff7d29b`, "struct's
# own remove() method call site mis-transpiled as Vec::remove"). That fix guarded the
# builtin Vec/HashMap/HashSet `.remove(...)` codegen on `!is_user_struct_receiver`, but
# `is_user_struct_receiver` (`expr_receiver_is_known_user_type` in
# src/transpiler/emit_methods.rs) resolved a `Var` receiver's type from `var_struct_types`/
# `var_types` alone -- it never saw through a `Res<T>`/`ResMut<T>` system-param wrapper the
# way `resolve_expr_struct_type` already does (see `TRANSPARENT_WRAPPER_GENERICS`, added
# for tests/cases/ext_res_field's field-access bug). So a call site like
# `widgets.remove(key)` where `widgets` is a `ResMut<Widgets>` system parameter -- the
# realistic, common shape for a Bevy resource written to -- still fell into the
# "must be Vec::remove(usize)" branch and wrapped the string key in a bogus
# negative-index-wrapping usize cast, even though `struct_custom_remove_call_site.br`'s
# bare-struct-receiver shape (`positions.remove(target_id)`, no wrapper) was already
# fixed.
#
# `ext_res.ResMut` (tests/cases/fixtures/ext_res) stands in for real bevy's `ResMut<T>` --
# a `Deref`/`DerefMut`-transparent wrapper around a real `T`, so `widgets.remove(key)` is a
# genuine call to `Widgets::remove` via auto-deref, and must compile -- not the Vec-style
# codegen, which doesn't compile here at all (`Widgets`/`ResMut<Widgets>` has no `.len()`,
# and `HashMap::remove` doesn't take a cast `usize`). `transpile_project_test!` (real
# `cargo run`) is needed for the same reason as `ext_res_field`: this is a codegen-only
# bug, `boring run`'s interpreter never resolves a `Res`/`ResMut` wrapper type at all.
use ext_res.ResMut

struct Widgets:
    var mut {string=int} table

    def remove(string key):
        table.remove(key)

def despawn(mut ResMut<Widgets> widgets):
    print widgets.table.len()
    widgets.remove("a")
    print widgets.table.len()

def main():
    var mut w = Widgets({=})
    w.table["a"] = 1
    w.table["b"] = 2
    despawn(ResMut(w))
